+/// What a call that looked for loops teaches the hold-off: a skip proves looking pays (reset); a call that skipped nothing although it did something observable or paid for lookups makes the next calls skip the looking, for longer each time in a row.
+/// The looking resumes by itself when the hold runs out, so detection is never switched off for good. (Only the choice of where to look changes; `prove_round` still alone authorises a skip.)
+fn settled_call_end(s: &mut Settled1, done: bool, wasted: bool) {
+    if done {
+        s.miss = 0;
+    } else if wasted {
+        s.miss = (s.miss + 1).min(SETTLED_MISS_MAX);
+        s.hold = (1u32 << s.miss) - 1;
+    }
